TCS Prime|TECHNICAL|System Design|4|Design a URL shortener supporting redirects and expiration. What data would you store and how would you handle collisions?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Unique short key; mapping; expiry; collision retry; caching.
TCS Prime|TECHNICAL|System Design|3|A background job may fail after partially completing its work. How would you make retries safe?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Idempotent operations; checkpoints; bounded retries and dead-letter queue.
TCS Prime|INTRO|Communication|1|Introduce yourself in about one minute, focusing on your education, technical interests and a project you are proud of.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Relevant concise introduction; concrete experience; clear structure.
TCS Prime|PROJECT|Projects|2|Choose one project you built. What problem did it solve, what was your contribution and how did you verify it worked?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Problem, ownership, implementation and evidence.
TCS Prime|PROJECT|Projects|3|Describe a difficult bug in a project you built. How did you reproduce, isolate and fix it?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Reproduction; diagnosis; fix; regression test.
TCS Prime|PROJECT|Projects|3|Choose a project you built. Why did you select its technology stack, and what alternative did you consider?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Concrete tradeoff and project constraints.
