Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Networks|3|A client receives HTTP 502 from a reverse proxy. What would you investigate first?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Upstream availability, connectivity, logs and timeouts.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Java|3|How does Java HashMap handle two unequal keys with the same hash code?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Bucket collision; equals; list/tree bins; resize considerations.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Java|2|Why should a mutable object generally not be used as a HashMap key?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Hash or equality changes break lookup consistency.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Java|3|What is the difference between checked and unchecked exceptions? Give an example of each.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Compile-time handling requirement; IOException versus runtime exceptions.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Python|2|Why does modifying a list assigned to another variable also affect the original variable?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Both references point to same mutable object; copying alternatives.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|Python|3|When would a generator be preferable to returning a list of all results?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Lazy iteration; reduced memory; single-pass tradeoffs.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|JavaScript|3|Why does a promise callback run after synchronous code even if the promise is already resolved?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Event loop; microtask queue; call stack.
Cognizant|TECHNICAL|JavaScript|2|What is the difference between let, const and var in JavaScript?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Block versus function scope; reassignment; hoisting and TDZ.
