Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|2|Given an array of integers and a target, how would you find two distinct indices whose values sum to the target?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Hash map of seen values; complement lookup; O(n) time and space.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|2|Given a string containing only parentheses, brackets and braces, determine whether every opening symbol is closed in the correct order.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Stack; matching closing symbol; reject leftover openings.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given a singly linked list, how can you determine whether it contains a cycle using constant extra space?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Floyd slow and fast pointers; meeting implies cycle.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given an array containing negative and positive integers, find the maximum sum of a nonempty contiguous subarray.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Kadane recurrence; initialize from first element; O(n).
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given a sorted array rotated at an unknown pivot with distinct values, find a target in logarithmic time.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Binary search; identify sorted half; narrow bounds.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|4|Given a directed graph of course prerequisites, return a valid course order or explain why none exists.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Topological sort; indegrees or DFS; cycle detection.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|4|Design a cache supporting get and put in constant time with least recently used eviction.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Hash map and doubly linked list; move on access; evict tail.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given a string, find the length of its longest substring without repeated characters.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Sliding window; last seen indices; O(n).
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|4|Given coin denominations and a target amount, find the minimum number of coins needed or report impossibility.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|DP over amounts; unreachable sentinel; unbounded transitions.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given a list of closed intervals, merge all overlapping intervals.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Sort by start; extend current end; O(n log n).
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|3|Given an unweighted graph, find the shortest path from vertex A to vertex B.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|BFS; visited set; parent reconstruction.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|DSA|4|Numbers arrive one at a time. How would you maintain their median after every insertion?|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Two heaps; balance sizes; median from roots.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|SQL|2|Employees(id, name, salary, department_id) stores employee records. Write a query to return the second highest distinct salary.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|DISTINCT with ordering and offset or MAX below maximum; handle missing result.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|SQL|3|Customers(id, name) and Orders(id, customer_id) are tables. Write a query returning customers who have never placed an order.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|NOT EXISTS or LEFT JOIN with null order id.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|SQL|3|Employees(id, department_id, salary) stores salaries. Return employees earning more than their own department average.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|Correlated subquery or window AVG partitioned by department.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|SQL|3|Orders(id, customer_id, amount) stores orders. Return customers whose total spending exceeds 10000.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|GROUP BY customer_id; SUM; HAVING.
Connecticus|TECHNICAL|SQL|4|Employees(id, department_id, salary) stores salaries. Return the three highest distinct salary ranks in each department, including ties.|ORIGINAL_PRACTICE||false|DENSE_RANK partition by department order by salary descending; filter rank.
